    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d179">

                <pb facs="0179" n="129" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg129"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2014</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-06-19T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 19, 1918,
                                3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your June 13, 5 p.m. Department believes reasonable quantity of material for
                    Moscow Supply Committee should be released and forwarded as trial shipment. When
                    shipment is made full information should be furnished Department to communicate
                    to consular representatives in Siberia and European Russia, so that they can
                    follow shipments to destination. Department has just approved shipment from this
                    country to Moscow Supply Committee 50,000 pairs shoes as trial shipment to be
                    delivered to representative of committee at Omsk.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
